#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198154 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198157 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c737d317-8e09-5ccb-b816-b5f56e925ba9" :question/math-academy-id "e-609" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198158 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cde8f304-4937-5eb7-a8e1-a08355ee4d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-611" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea0caa8a-efee-56d7-bcba-88fab2c4cc9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296280} {:answer/id #uuid "feb420f5-92f6-50f8-9f43-b14a9faed5d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296281} {:answer/id #uuid "daa56bde-0ca1-5908-a8a5-dc39f006622f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296282} {:answer/id #uuid "b765b9fb-44c6-5bff-a7bf-d24be9b68e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2t-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296283} {:answer/id #uuid "b0918c43-5799-55a5-85a1-82fcfde2f444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daa56bde-0ca1-5908-a8a5-dc39f006622f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296282} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd48b67-6cfd-533d-b1fc-b4bc48bff2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f7fd91d-2382-5008-942f-17ee55f68071" :question/math-academy-id "q-123167" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)={t}^{2}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2t-1 \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335727a5-171c-5077-8b97-40a626e083e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}\\,i-12\\,j-\\frac{3}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296287} {:answer/id #uuid "d38d8e55-b4d6-5c18-9afa-bbc43673d8cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}\\,i-6\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296288} {:answer/id #uuid "848e8751-d500-58e3-a7a4-d67cb8f3929e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}\\,i-3\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296289} {:answer/id #uuid "85f2a729-0064-5a94-babd-5a56b0664e77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}\\,i-12\\,j-\\frac{4}{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296290} {:answer/id #uuid "1eeb747a-b0fb-5b9b-a2fd-e5fdab470eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3}\\,i-8\\,j+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "335727a5-171c-5077-8b97-40a626e083e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}\\,i-12\\,j-\\frac{3}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296287} :answer-field/id #uuid "21ea7ecd-ca3b-5564-b42d-4a2135378961" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26a29b71-03ad-558b-a306-d8c279ec3ed6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130405" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=t{e}^{t}\\,i-3{t}^{2}\\,j+\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}\\,k$ at $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}})k \\\\  & =(t+1){e}^{t}\\,i-6t\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{3}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(2)$ we substitute $t=2$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =(2+1){e}^{2}\\,i-6(2)\\,j-\\frac{6}{{2}^{3}}\\,k \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}\\,i-12\\,j-\\frac{3}{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "febe63d1-d258-5e53-8cd7-df14721779c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296294} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4da0d5-d11d-5a05-9393-b4e5c11f64e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296295} {:answer/id #uuid "047ed2f6-8004-52b3-8a77-de566d78b8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296296} {:answer/id #uuid "d4facdb8-8040-5f7f-a9d4-be02d82fb92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296297} {:answer/id #uuid "31f56289-278f-5f45-918a-28ca47d53d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "047ed2f6-8004-52b3-8a77-de566d78b8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296296} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8fadb71-0f6a-5185-bb76-b05264c49d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f56cbc0a-b886-55fd-8b4c-e347c18369ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-32280" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(\\pi )$ if $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -6({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}^{″}(\\pi )$ by substituting $t=\\pi $ into the above:\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi  \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-(-1)-0 \\\\ -6\\cdot 1 \\\\ -4\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb4e788e-497f-5bc5-ac41-a16fba649e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{1-{t}^{2}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296301} {:answer/id #uuid "226941c1-86e3-56cf-b213-6033afdc0d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j+\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296302} {:answer/id #uuid "56101fe4-94ba-5155-a1fa-d0c1ebc68736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-5{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296303} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe41cfd-acdb-523f-b4b9-ac721119bcc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296304} {:answer/id #uuid "bc121725-d27a-5776-b5c2-408b4a1936a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fe41cfd-acdb-523f-b4b9-ac721119bcc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296304} :answer-field/id #uuid "6246727a-8ca6-516c-8057-0376c8e2ff53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f9e4927-ed2e-5650-ac36-cbfcaf27d88b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32417" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡3t\\,i-5{t}^{4}\\,j+\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$  by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡3t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "315c480a-eb74-576b-b27b-1fb21b42a3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-2{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296308} {:answer/id #uuid "37bf8dad-c47f-5a8e-9fd2-777a6ae4a49c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }\\,i-{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296309} {:answer/id #uuid "a2231bd2-b528-56d7-89eb-bfef3d43e984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296310} {:answer/id #uuid "f7fe3dbd-ed7b-57b2-810b-edd626454def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296311} {:answer/id #uuid "865525ca-4942-5c39-8fb3-c877b988de32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7fe3dbd-ed7b-57b2-810b-edd626454def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296311} :answer-field/id #uuid "4179a45a-2092-56a5-81b2-ad63ba7d5787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e579ce0-d5f9-57b8-931d-2fc18fc335d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-34724" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ at $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =({e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+({e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{\\pi }\\cdot 0+{e}^{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+({e}^{\\pi }\\cdot (-1)-{e}^{\\pi }\\cdot 0)\\,k \\\\  & =-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c44c3ea-3ebf-5ee5-af0a-8110ad679376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c44c3ea-3ebf-5ee5-af0a-8110ad679376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296315} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf779698-c2ba-5641-af73-001c287ae21b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69e2c430-6329-572d-a61d-182cbabbb01a" :question/math-academy-id "q-347617" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨7-3t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(1)|?$\n\n$|{r}^{′}(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=7-3t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=-3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=2{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=4t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=4(1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad315727-eb7f-5354-bbab-439e06f75dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296318} {:answer/id #uuid "67e714c1-d19a-50ee-841f-16500ad16c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e714c1-d19a-50ee-841f-16500ad16c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296319} :answer-field/id #uuid "0af204b7-e80e-517b-b400-b842c5391472" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d34acfc3-184b-5280-bb18-fba11290bc23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d34acfc3-184b-5280-bb18-fba11290bc23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296321} :answer-field/id #uuid "f091808e-591c-5385-9455-31e4b75a7ff2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7fd9ec9-3859-5d29-8534-5127f6943be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7fd9ec9-3859-5d29-8534-5127f6943be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296323} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea80d0f1-98f5-55e5-8139-4f5771d7f77f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7302653-c201-588a-9a11-bdd609a1f5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-347628" :question/problem "Given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t),\\,{t}^{3}⟩,$ what is ${f}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5abf2d8-c8a4-5524-9322-11275d512b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296326} {:answer/id #uuid "4afc81d1-1742-588d-af02-c1806d222f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5abf2d8-c8a4-5524-9322-11275d512b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296326} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a82e46e-061b-598b-9edc-e29e6ec5b771" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04818994-d6d9-5b40-984b-58d918b92e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04818994-d6d9-5b40-984b-58d918b92e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296329} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdebd735-4aed-511f-9364-c21a3d0dde07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18dc3f26-327b-53a4-8232-4e313a8b13d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-349469" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(0)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(0)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{2t}(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(2{e}^{2t})(t+1)+{e}^{2t}(1) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(t+1)+{e}^{2t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(0)=2{e}^{2\\cdot 0}(0+1)+{e}^{2\\cdot 0}=3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{9-{0}^{2}}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{x}^{′}(0),\\,{y}^{′}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9c019d-977f-5955-8493-e435a22e1136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296332} {:answer/id #uuid "e82b5f7b-9696-54e1-b1a2-95d4e3187636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296333} {:answer/id #uuid "8b48747b-b226-59e5-9900-3670f65971fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296334} {:answer/id #uuid "04998e9f-9e01-5cf2-a2ca-fc4b21c24bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296335} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b068f2-cbe7-5bf9-b70d-dadaf841489f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e82b5f7b-9696-54e1-b1a2-95d4e3187636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296333} :answer-field/id #uuid "29ae8b6c-f927-5354-bb2a-e924f52b4e33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54" :question/math-academy-id "q-50371" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} {:answer/id #uuid "a02992c9-bb0d-53e8-8eee-9ab879a36726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296340} {:answer/id #uuid "5af4e518-15cd-5056-b76e-8979a49a9066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296341} {:answer/id #uuid "499b53ad-0f19-573e-9e6f-6c6b1e5c759d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296342} {:answer/id #uuid "7d81d374-3be8-5dad-bad8-7bbfcbcd0fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe23e1b9-a6e4-5d5c-acb8-5f1d8899b18b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eef8652-af24-51e5-8f51-46e17a486c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-50373" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e066582-5eca-5419-a495-6965c1800f41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296346} {:answer/id #uuid "71d744fe-2f62-5cf8-8f81-87a43426ed95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296347} {:answer/id #uuid "c25ec7de-12af-529c-af44-a22fc24a0151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296348} {:answer/id #uuid "0534d891-006d-5d29-a9ad-aa1a973dfd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296349} {:answer/id #uuid "3a27fa3f-430b-59a5-bfa0-477b70d9a00b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0534d891-006d-5d29-a9ad-aa1a973dfd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296349} :answer-field/id #uuid "b53136bb-c75f-5654-a83c-966336d9efc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "189c2727-12a4-5484-ae84-df807a41b9e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-50409" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={sin}^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={cos}^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8306d7b-85f8-5c1b-a31f-d3a5e16f0087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296353} {:answer/id #uuid "05e9aa89-4d5c-5e02-8f43-31eb797d14c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296354} {:answer/id #uuid "88b820fa-1a16-517f-9da7-1c476ae063dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296355} {:answer/id #uuid "40615f60-9250-598b-9235-610cc0e94635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296356} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7c8b52-a41b-595d-af0d-30a2a3fc1d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b820fa-1a16-517f-9da7-1c476ae063dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296355} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd690fd1-0f1b-5fc3-8cdd-13ca7633556c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fd0a18c-43f2-5761-ad4b-96e6a87257fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-50467" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6768e3e-c0e0-58f5-a6f0-c7316661b894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-10{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296360} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2718ae-b57e-557d-b895-ae7069cf41e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296361} {:answer/id #uuid "6588280c-67ff-592b-a7b4-ba8e5d8a27fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j+20{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296362} {:answer/id #uuid "fe26d7af-11cc-5520-8d93-26e93308c32b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j+20{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296363} {:answer/id #uuid "03fdb001-9fcc-56f9-98c8-c7a5a29115d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2718ae-b57e-557d-b895-ae7069cf41e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296361} :answer-field/id #uuid "d880a43d-7e0b-53bc-b672-d28bf0076e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5854a1fc-01c0-5fc6-8d85-2b342d3dc37f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69907" :question/problem "Find the second derivative of $f(t)={e}^{3t+2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-2{t}^{5}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t+2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{5})\\,k \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+(-2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j+(-2\\cdot 5{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j-10{t}^{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{3t+2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-10{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3(3{e}^{3t+2})\\,i-2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,j-10(4{t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd0aa54e-b500-5291-be3e-5e6deae95540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}},\\,\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296367} {:answer/id #uuid "ea04a700-d4a1-5333-82e1-d5470f7ab098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{-3}{t+1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296368} {:answer/id #uuid "d73d67dd-6669-5d22-ae3d-66d87b4962d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296369} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d2b0e9-a81c-5f06-9560-dcc520d49aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296370} {:answer/id #uuid "9c3d50c3-e65d-5d7e-b70a-206f4550fe6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{-1}{t+1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2d2b0e9-a81c-5f06-9560-dcc520d49aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296370} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8de9187-2c1c-5a2d-946c-42e9d3657f57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40db78a3-8e98-5f3c-8f6f-0721104f563f" :question/math-academy-id "q-75034" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{3}{t+1} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc9fa57d-66de-5ae8-b713-739c4f41a695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296374} {:answer/id #uuid "3691eb0d-41b6-5f38-aba7-6a75c98d9238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296375} {:answer/id #uuid "5a0a29df-01e9-57fb-a254-e2203c7df4c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+2\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296376} {:answer/id #uuid "c87b2c75-19a3-5ffa-868a-e8f9e6737165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296377} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc01904-7be4-5bcc-ab41-764af5591260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c87b2c75-19a3-5ffa-868a-e8f9e6737165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296377} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0aac82-7a4e-5d3e-8988-838b31f9f3ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d9f58cb-435d-56fa-87f4-3623cbee5471" :question/math-academy-id "q-77678" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{1}{1+t}\\,k$ at $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{1+t})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,i+(6t-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+t)^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1)$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{1+(1)^{2}}\\,i+(6(1)-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+(1))^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
